      {
         "id": "SECTION_prerequisites",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Prerequisites\n\nThis game practices the ideas from the text *Always present* (<htcite0>). Before playing, read that text to understand how dividing by 3 is the same as organizing what we have into groups of three.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a9086b63-70d4-4984-a353-1118305128b6",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Always present",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_game",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Game\n\nA set of elements appears: they can be fruits, stars, cats, triangles or dogs. The total is always a multiple of three — 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18, 21, 24, 27 or 30. Your task is to say into how many groups of three these elements can be organized (<htcite0>).\n\nUse the buttons to choose the number of groups. There are three levels: the first asks from 1 to 3 groups, the second from 4 to 6, and the third from 7 to 10. The multiplication table of 3 is shown on the side to help you (<htcite1>).",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a9086b63-70d4-4984-a353-1118305128b6",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Always present",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "72dcaa0f-07e3-41de-a637-c5b2f528dc33",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Understanding the Multiplication Table (2 and 3)",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<div class=\"htGroupThreesGame\"><div class=\"htGroupThreesColumns\"><div class=\"htGroupThreesPlay\"><span class=\"htGroupThreesLevel\" id=\"htGroupThreesLevel\"></span><span class=\"htGroupThreesQuestion\" id=\"htGroupThreesQuestion\">In how many groups of 3 can we organize these elements?</span><span class=\"htGroupThreesTotal\" id=\"htGroupThreesTotal\"></span><div class=\"htGroupThreesElements\" id=\"htGroupThreesElements\"></div><div class=\"htGroupThreesButtonsRow\" id=\"htGroupThreesButtons\"></div><div class=\"htGroupThreesFeedback\" id=\"htGroupThreesFeedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><div class=\"htGroupThreesNextContainer\"><button type=\"button\" id=\"htGroupThreesNewBtn\" class=\"reset-tutor-btn\">🎲 New exercise</button><button type=\"button\" id=\"htGroupThreesNextBtn\" class=\"reset-tutor-btn hidden\">Next level</button></div></div><div class=\"htGroupThreesTable\"><span class=\"htGroupThreesTableTitle\">Multiplication Table of 3</span><div id=\"mParent3\"></div></div></div><span id=\"htGroupThreesLevelTemplate\" class=\"htGroupThreesHidden\">Level {n} of 3</span><span id=\"htGroupThreesTotalTemplate\" class=\"htGroupThreesHidden\">Total of {total} elements</span><span id=\"htGroupThreesMsgCorrect\" class=\"htGroupThreesHidden\">🎉 Congratulations! The {total} elements, grouped in threes, form {groups} groups. So {total} = 3 × {groups}.</span><span id=\"htGroupThreesMsgWrong\" class=\"htGroupThreesHidden\">Not yet. Each group holds 3 elements. Count how many groups of three fit inside {total} and try again.</span><span id=\"htGroupThreesMsgFinal\" class=\"htGroupThreesHidden\">🎉🎉🎉 Congratulations! You completed all the levels! 🎉🎉🎉</span><span id=\"htGroupThreesPlayAgain\" class=\"htGroupThreesHidden\">Play again</span><span id=\"htGroupThreesNextLabel\" class=\"htGroupThreesHidden\">Next level</span></div>",
